Verbatim ACAgent output:
OOLITE_CALL_FUNCTION_BEGIN
OOLITE_JS_CALL_FUNCTION setup=0 codes=0,1,0 sum=15 recovered=20 rpc=2 done=3 closed=1 status=PASS
OOLITE_CALL_FUNCTION_RC 0
OOLITE_CALL_FUNCTION_END

The C source-level adapter accepts an opaque borrowed JS function, receiver,
arguments and returns an owned JSValue (not a SpiderMonkey jsval word). JS_Call
ran on the script task while the original game-task Exec port pumped ship
property requests. Function returned {sum: 2+3+ship.bounty,tag:'cobra'} and
the caller decoded sum=15 after JS_Post completion. A deliberate exception
returned JSERR_EXCEPTION=1 without a returned value, and an independent
script afterwards returned ship.bounty*2=20. Two game task RPCs, three DONE
messages, clean shutdown.

This does not implement original OOJavaScriptEngine.m or its full class and
GC-root management. It qualifies the replacement invocation contract.
